AGF-NG licence summary
======================

Copyright (c) 2026 Jani Paijanen

AGF-NG uses more than one licence because the repository contains both
framework content and implementation tooling.

Framework and governance content
--------------------------------

The adopter-facing framework, governance rules, agent definitions, schemas,
documentation, examples, plans, proposals, and coordination records are
licensed under:

  Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-SA-4.0

The canonical product licence text is in:

  agf/LICENSE

Full legal text:

  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode

Tooling
-------

Implementation tooling intended to be embedded, modified, or redistributed as
software is licensed under:

  MIT License
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

The canonical tooling licence text is in:

  agf/LICENSE-MIT

Other licence terms
-------------------

Some framework artifacts are marked as available under:

  CC-BY-SA-4.0 OR LicenseRef-AgentsGovern-Commercial

Commercial or otherwise separate licence terms may be available by agreement
with the copyright holder. Those terms are alternatives to the public licence
where expressly granted; they are not implied by this summary.

Trademarks and third-party names
--------------------------------

All product names, service names, company names, logos, and trademarks
mentioned in this project are the property of their respective owners.
References to them are for identification and descriptive purposes only
and do not imply any endorsement, sponsorship, affiliation, or
partnership.

This project is developed independently and has no official relationship
with the owners of those trademarks.

Bootstrap reference
-------------------

The `agents-govern/` directory is a bootstrap reference copy used to govern
this project's development. Its own licence files and headers remain part of
that reference distribution.

When a file has an SPDX header, that header is authoritative for that file.
When there is no file-specific header, use the path-based summary above.
